# Build output — regenerated by `npm run build`, never edited by hand.
dist/

# Astro's generated types and content cache.
.astro/

# Dependencies. `npm install` restores them from package-lock.json.
node_modules/

# Logs
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
pnpm-debug.log*
*.log

# Environment
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Editor and OS clutter
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp

# ── DELIBERATELY NOT IGNORED ──────────────────────────────────────────
# The six *-backup files at the root are committed rather than ignored. They
# are point-in-time snapshots taken before risky edits, from before there was
# any version control — nothing imports them and the build ignores them. This
# first commit keeps them so it is a faithful snapshot of the folder; now that
# the history exists they are redundant and can be deleted whenever you like.
#
# _originals/ is 34MB of untouched source media for two works. Source, not
# output — it stays.
#
# build12.py / chrome12.py / css12.py at the root are dead scaffolding from an
# earlier generator workflow. build12.py imports a module (inner7) that is not
# in the folder, so it cannot even run. Kept for history, safe to delete.
#
# src/media/ is ~279MB of stills. That is source material, not build
# output: every work page and the mosaic bed are built from it, Astro
# optimises it at build time into dist/, and there is no other copy. It
# has to be in the history. No single file exceeds 7.5MB, so nothing here
# comes near GitHub's 100MB limit — but the repo is large, so a first
# clone will take a while.
